{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism","id":113651,"title":"Solar Transhumanism?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-15T16:53:40-07:00","id":113651,"title":"Solar Transhumanism?","content":"There's an old quote somewhere on the old forums about a Solar who goes searching for cosmic transcendence and eventually figures out that he already has it by virtue of being a Solar. This has always struck me as a cop-out when compared to &quot;real&quot; transhumanists who have mechanical support for their transformations into &quot;something else&quot; like the Infernals and Alchemicals. Could someone explain to me where this position comes from? I have difficulty seeing how a Solar can be called transhuman any more than Batman or Son Goku can be called such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","user":"HK-87","date":". 04-15-2014, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:06:29-07:00","id":113663,"title":"","content":"Transhumanism isn't really something Exalted is about, and as such, it's a concept the Solars don't really have a direct buy-in into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:28:28-07:00","id":113672,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's sort of a cop-out, in the sense of &quot;achieving immortality through the memories of others.&quot; But that goal is going to be kind of like chasing the pot of gold at the end of the rainbow, so I can't really fault anyone who decides at some point, &quot;The real pot of gold was in me all along! What a relief, I'm gonna go home and take a shower.&quot;<br /> <br /> I sort of think of the &quot;weird, busted&quot; Exalted -- the Abyssals and Infernals -- as the ones you go to for transhuman themes, by virtue of the fact that they're kind of alien and &quot;unstable&quot; and evoke themes otherwise at odds with the nature of Exaltation. Alchemicals sort of apply, I guess -- mentally I tended to exclude them because the transhumanist narrative tends to be strongly individualist and Alchemicals start out fairly un-individualist and become less so as they mature, but it fits.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's ever going to be anything but at odds with Solar motifs, though. Solars are the <i>most</i> human Exalted, and transhumanism comes from a place of deep dissatisfaction and disenchantment with humanity and humanism. A Solar is never going to be able to step away from their basic humanity the way an Abyssal can -- they might become weird or terrible, but not in a transhuman way. This is so integral to what &quot;being a Solar&quot; is that I would probably say that any decisive success at overcoming it would involve either shedding your Exaltation or becoming a different sort of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:29:05-07:00","id":113673,"title":"","content":"I'm not tremendously well informed on transhumanist culture, but from what I can see, at least some of their objectives can be achieved by means of Solar Charms, in the sense of transcending the limitations of their human bodies and minds.<br /> <br /> Jumping over mountains, running faster than a car, seeing things that are invisible to normal humans, manipulating the fundamental forces of the universe to create stable reality from unreal chaos...there is a lot of stuff in the Solar charmset that fits within the desires of few transhumanists with which I have talked about it or whose desires I've read about. You know, the guys who go &quot;I wish I could see the full electromagnetic spectrum instead of seeing the universe with these limited human eyes&quot;. Essence Sight is a decent analogue to that in Exalted.<br /> <br /> We look at genetic manipulation or trading our bodies for machines and things like that as a way to leave aside many of the worries and limitations of humanity, but when you have Solar magic on your side, you don't necessarily have to look for something weird in order to achieve that.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I have misunderstood something, though. When some people talk about it, it seems they want to be fundamentally different from humans, while other simply seem to want to be able to do things humans cannot, cases in which makes it hard for me to find the distinction between transhuman and superhuman.<br /> <br /> I mean, ok, a Solar probably doesn't do the equivalent of uploading his personality into a network of computers to expand their mind beyond the human limit, but he could probably achieve any of the end results (amazing amounts of knowledge, calculating things at incredible speeds) by just &quot;being really freaking knowledgeable and enlightened&quot;. He won't turn his eyes into cyber multi-spectrum-binoculars/microscopes, but he can see great distances or very small things or in the dark or the energy the makes up all things all the same, and so on. What is it that constitutes transhumanism, beyond the transcending of normal human capacities and limitations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:35:02-07:00","id":113676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=113663#post113663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transhumanism isn't really something Exalted is about, and as such, it's a concept the Solars don't really have a direct buy-in into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not like a charm or a devil-tiger path, no, but apparently it's something they can do. I started thinking about this because I found an old post (old like 2009 or so) on RPG.net from... Neall? I don't know all the writers by name yet, but he's one of the freelancers I think. Here it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More specifically, every type of Exalt has a method they can approach transhumanism through. Terrestrials can emulate the Dragons and incorporate more elements; Lunars have chimerism; Sidereals are mostly stuck, but can embrace martial arts; Abyssals can become Deathlords, Infernals <b>*redacted*</b> and Alchemicals can become cities.<br /> <br /> Solars are just less obvious than the others (the Adamant Caste too, actually, now that I think about it). I think your artifact method is a good way, even if it's treading a bit on the Alchemicals. Another way - and if Matthias comes along, he'll do this idea justice - would be the sort of Great Leader archetype, imprinting your thoughts and desires on everyone you rule over, so you're as integral a part of their daily life as their family. By tying their emotional state into your own, you become a sort of societal entity, a living nation, and your Solar form is but an avatar. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:47:36-07:00","id":113683,"title":"","content":"You know, I've talked at length in the past about my personal disdain verging on contempt for transhumanism, but it's only recently that I've found myself able to articulate why in the simple terms of my categorically rejecting humanism, which transhumanism intrinsically relies upon (you can only assert that technological or other modifications will make somebody &quot;beyond human&quot; if you subscribe to an exclusive model of what a human being is).<br /> <br /> When Exalted has stuff like beastfolk, and indeed the Exalted themselves, I perceive it to be a fairly antihumanist game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:50:25-07:00","id":113687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=113676#post113676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not like a charm or a devil-tiger path, no, but apparently it's something they can do. I started thinking about this because I found an old post (old like 2009 or so) on RPG.net from... Neall? I don't know all the writers by name yet, but he's one of the freelancers I think. Here it is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, what's described could rather easily be done with some custom charms building off of Sun King Radiance and Socialize or Performance.<br /> (and potentially those mote-capacity-boosting charms that require you to take care of bureaucracies/societies/etc.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T17:58:22-07:00","id":113696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=113683#post113683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I've talked at length in the past about my personal disdain verging on contempt for transhumanism, but it's only recently that I've found myself able to articulate why in the simple terms of my categorically rejecting humanism, which transhumanism intrinsically relies upon (you can only assert that technological or other modifications will make somebody &quot;beyond human&quot; if you subscribe to an exclusive model of what a human being is).<br /> <br /> When Exalted has stuff like beastfolk, and indeed the Exalted themselves, I perceive it to be a fairly antihumanist game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You... reject humanism? I didn't know people did that. And I really don't see how beastfolks make the Exalted antihumanist. <br /> <br /> I mean, &quot;self-realization through reason&quot; and &quot;human beings have dignity and worth&quot; are not elements Exalted specifically rejects...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:24:25-07:00","id":113724,"title":"","content":"Humanism also includes assertions of an ideal, exclusive and universal model for what humans either are, or should be.<br /> <br /> Which... actually kind of encompasses the ideas of self-realization through reason and that they all have dignity and worth.<br /> <br /> This is not me saying that humans can't or shouldn't self-realize through reason, mind, just that self-realization is not an ideal goal for every human, nor that it is only or ideally acquired through reason*.<br /> <br /> Likewise, if I view not every human to have dignity or (to the extent that such a subjective value can even be meaningfully ascribed in the first place) &quot;worth&quot;, that is not me saying that it's okay to mistreat or otherwise degrade people who might be viewed as lacking those qualities.<br /> <br /> Antihumanism does not mean being anti human, it means being anti the philosophy of humanism.<br /> <br /> I reject humanism because I find the impulse to find a universal standard of what humans are or should be to be somewhere between misguided and logically inconsistent (I look out upon the rich varied tapestry of what human beings are and see neither worth nor possibility of success in attempting to box it all up in uniformity), and because, at worst, I view it as a preface to defining models of humanity specifically designed around marginalizing people who do not and cannot fit into them under a pretext of rationality.<br /> <br /> It's why I reject reference to even the most terrible people as &quot;inhuman&quot; in all but the most poetic terms (especially as regards the concept of &quot;if you act 'inhumanly' you waive your entitlement to human rights and dignity&quot;, one of the more odious arguments for varying kinds of brutalization of convicted criminals).<br /> <br /> Humans are anything they have been, anything they are, and anything they can be.<br /> <br /> You're no less human for having had an ancestor who was a snake, or having better physical hardiness or restoration, or having been an active part of a culture that thought throwing a bag of cats into a bonfire was a good larf.<br /> <br /> I find no credibility in transhumanism, because I find no credibility to the idea that any qualities that such modifications might provide are exclusive from the condition of being human.<br /> <br /> Hence, a Solar is no transhuman for anything provided by their Charms, by their Sorcery, by any internal or external artifacts they might possess.<br /> <br /> Some of the terminology John has used in the past actually lines in neatly with this perspective I'm developing; I'm growing to prefer to articulate Solars as being less obliquely magical than (in a setting where the lack of oblique magic was initial a severe disadvantage of humanity) over Solars as being &quot;most human&quot; of the Exalted, since I shouldn't really view the latter term as making much sense, and even kind of detracting from the other Exalted. Likewise with the idea that there's a necessary core of humanity to Terrestrials and all other Exalted.<br /> <br /> * In the context of Exalted, I feel as though the Infernals and possibly Lunars might be fairly explicit in form of self-realization that are achieved through... means other than reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:33:48-07:00","id":113728,"title":"","content":"Transhumanism is an intellectual movement that aims at transforming the nature of human life,<i> i.e.</i> the human condition. An example of transhumanism in Exalted would be a circle of super high-essence Solar sorcerers doing some kind of 'working' that abolished death and made everyone immortal. That'd be transhumanism because it'd transform the very nature of human existence. The kinds of personal transformation that Infernals and Lunars can undergo, while cool, don't really seem on the same level. They're personal-scale transformations, and even if the end is becoming something vastly more powerful and even different, how transhuman it is in terms of results really seems to vary widely according to how it's played.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-15-2014, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T18:56:00-07:00","id":113742,"title":"","content":"Transhumanism is kind of this big lump of a term that a lot of different ideas get tossed into.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about transhumanism in the sense of you, personally, surpassing the limits of humanity by becoming &quot;human plus&quot;, then that's literally every Exaltation. All of them come with a centuries-long lifespan minimum, superhuman physical abilities, and in most cases superhuman mental abilities as well. You don't even need to buy any Charms to be transhuman under that definition.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about transhumanism in the sense of becoming something that is distinctly inhuman, then that's Lunar chimerism or Infernals. This concept of transhumanism really doesn't have much to do with the others, though.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about transhumanism in the sense of improving the entirety of the human condition through technology, then no Exaltation does that. Exaltation is generally a very self-centered thing. Some sort of artifact construction or sorcerous working could deal with this type of transhumanism in theory, but it's not at all material covered by any of the Exalts. The only exception would be if the Dragon-Blooded had a way of guaranteeing Exaltation in a way that they could over time replace all humans everywhere with Dragon-Blooded. That would generally fit that model of transhumanism, but again it's something that would probably be accomplished through creating an artifact system to do so or performing some sort of great sorcery, rather than something within the Exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T07:07:41-07:00","id":114037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=113663#post113663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transhumanism isn't really something Exalted is about, and as such, it's a concept the Solars don't really have a direct buy-in into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on your definition of transhumanism. You could also see every Solar becoming a transhumanist after he solved all his previously (to his Exaltation) open problems and is learning that he is not mere human anymore. Both in body and in mind, because an immortal being with theoretically unknown limits of power cannot work with a basic human way of thinking for long. Every Exalt transcends his human ideals and also ideas after some time.<br /> <br /> That being said, Solars are very external in that regard. Most of their Charms allow them to be leaders, teachers and builders. Shinmaic Callibration is a similar external process of transcendence but without needing a nation / group to lead. The Salinan Working is one fluffelement that shows what Solar transcendence is all about<b></b>: Changing the world. Sometimes literally by changing its settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T07:10:42-07:00","id":114039,"title":"","content":"At some point that I must have missed, transhumanism seems to have become something mandatory, expected and important. I'm rather confused as to why or how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T07:59:27-07:00","id":114062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114039#post114039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point that I must have missed, transhumanism seems to have become something mandatory, expected and important. I'm rather confused as to why or how.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because deciding that you're not satisfied with what you are and pushing for another step is extremely cool and Infernals (and Alchemicals, if you think turning into a city is cool rather than lame) shouldn't be the only splat to have all the fun with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:11:38-07:00","id":114068,"title":"","content":"Interesting that this came up. Last night, I posted to my art blog a picture of my custom Deathlord who accidentally killed himself a few decades before the Usurpation, trying to make a robot body, but in the process trapped his now-dormant Exaltation in that robot body, and provided the first practical demonstration for the Sidereals that something like the Jade Prison was even possible. He was mostly intended as a cautionary tale about throwing out the baby (Solar Exaltation) with the bathwater (not being a gross assembly of meat and hair that won't stop secreting, excreting, bleeding, shedding, and exhaling all over things).<br /> <br /> I think transhumanism is a thing Solars can explore, because it's a thing Humans can explore. Therefore, a Solar who gets it into his head to start shedding the traits of mere mortals is going to do a pretty boss job of it. To a certain extent, the story of jaded immortals becoming distant from their roots will automatically be similar. But it's not a default path, or one that would come across as particularly enlightened. If a Solar says &quot;I want to be a Robot&quot;, he can do that, and probably make it work. If a Solar says &quot;I want to become some kind of weird space octopus&quot;, there's probably a path available. If a Solar says &quot;I want to become free of need and want, tranquil and centered, and sit on a mountain for a thousand years without eating or sleeping or breathing or blinking&quot;, that's a thing that he can do. It's good for everybody to have a hobby, is what I'm trying to say. The same Solar could say &quot;I want to become SO GOOD at playing Poker, holy crap!&quot; and dumps a thousand years of downtime EXP into custom card shark charms, if they wanted to. Sometimes people get crazy focused on one weird goal, and lose sight of everything else. That's absolutely a place Old Solars can and should go, if they like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:21:46-07:00","id":114081,"title":"","content":"Transhumanism, in Exalted discussion, takes you to weird places because you're taking an idea and trying to shoehorn it into an RPG.<br /> <br /> It's generally used as shorthand for, &quot;Beyond Human&quot; but you can already do that. Exalted can get say, an Intelligence of 6 or 7, much higher than any normal human. That's some personal &quot;transhumanism&quot; right there.<br /> <br /> But that's not what most people mean. They tend to mean charms or effects that significantly alter the nature of your character, mechanically.<br /> <br /> People have been discussing this sort of idea for a while (some of the Abyssal Taint charms can start modifying your character like that) but it wasn't until we got Infernals however that the idea of &quot;transhumanism&quot; got coined, so it's generally safe to point towards those effects.<br /> <br /> Things like the Ebon Dragon charm which allows you to permanently sacrifice your virtues, or the SWLiHN charm which allows you to push your virtues to 6 but makes it very difficult to go against them, or the Malfeas Charm which forces you to reject anybody who tries to express authority over you.<br /> <br /> When discussing &quot;transhumanism&quot; in Exalted it's generally a good idea to think of those permanent duration charms with extreme effects that change very fundamental aspects of your character.<br /> <br /> I don't think that they're mandatory for all splats though.<br /> <br /> Sidereal and Lunars can mess around with temporary &quot;transhumanism&quot; (Sidereal MA for Sidereals and various Knacks for Lunars). Abyssals, Infernals and Alchemicals all have varying degrees of this at play in their charmsets. We'll probably see something crop up in Liminals, and I am sure there will be some Exigents that can make use of this concept. Who knows about Gentimians, I wouldn't be surprised either way. Other Exalted, not so much. Which seems fine to me. It's not a niche that is terribly important or necessary for all of the Exalted to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:49:38-07:00","id":114100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114081#post114081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or the SWLiHN charm which allows you to push your virtues to 6 but makes it very difficult to go against them...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it keeps it at 5, it just turns the relevant dice to auto-successes any time they'd be rolled.[/QUOTE]If you want a Virtue at 6, you'd need to delve into Scroll of Heroes for that one stupid Merit, or pick up a Green Iron Heart if it's Conviction you want at 6.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:52:52-07:00","id":114103,"title":"","content":"I think people suddenly being so interested in transhumanism is yet another facet of Infernals stealing the show with their nonstandard design. It worked for them, because it makes sense that humans being granted the power of the most inhuman beings in the setting would lead to shedding/losing humanity. At the same time, the Infernals were somewhat &quot;incomplete&quot; (though in retrospect, this perception wasn't so much implicated in their design as outright hinted in plain text), and thus they got the option to &quot;complete&quot; their transformation and become Devil-Tigers. Which was fun. For them. In the context of the game late 2e became. And since it was fun, everyone wanted to get in on the action. Let it stew in the echo chamber for a few months, and suddenly transhumanism is a big theme of Exalted, not just of 2e Infernals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:03:14-07:00","id":114113,"title":"","content":"One thing I notice about discussions of what is or is not correct or thematic for a given type of Exalt is that they often hinge on arguments about things that only become possible for that Exalt at super high essence. Devil-tiger, for instance, can't happen until Essence 6, well beyond the level of 99% of Exalted games. And on this thread, we've fallen into the trap of discussing what a group of high-essence Solars could do with the greatest act of sorcery ever.<br /> <br /> I really wish Essence 6 had never even been addressed in charm sets, because this is what it does. It makes it very difficult to even talk about the setting in a way that applies to the vast majority of games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:06:57-07:00","id":114117,"title":"","content":"Actually it's even worse than that; it convinced people that Essence 6+ Exalted was the <i>real</i> game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:07:43-07:00","id":114119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114103#post114103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people suddenly being so interested in transhumanism is yet another facet of Infernals stealing the show with their nonstandard design. It worked for them, because it makes sense that humans being granted the power of the most inhuman beings in the setting would lead to shedding/losing humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of devil-tigers is that they keep their humanity while also growing beyond the limitations of it, unlike the yozis which are limited to being alien-minded idiot-savants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:14:53-07:00","id":114123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114119#post114119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of devil-tigers is that they keep their humanity while also growing beyond the limitations of it, unlike the yozis which are limited to being alien-minded idiot-savants.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's cool, but in the standard setting, no Infernal has ever become a devil-tiger. It's literally something that doesn't even apply to Infernals, <u>unless</u> it's an Infernals game and it's being played at a high enough level that the game is to a certain extent broken already. And even then, it would only apply to a minority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-16-2014, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:28:57-07:00","id":114131,"title":"","content":"So what you're saying is that no Infernal's ever become a Devil-Tiger, except for the ones who have.<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;standard&quot; game, TSk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:36:47-07:00","id":114135,"title":"","content":"I said standard <u>setting.</u> When the game begins, by default in RY 768, I think it's canonical that no Infernals have actually become devil-tigers, and it's possible that none ever will. If they do, it's because of ST fiat or player action. My point being that it's unfortunate (IMO) that something that doesn't apply to the vast majority of Exalts of a certain type comes to define that type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-16-2014, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:38:44-07:00","id":114137,"title":"","content":"Edit: ninja'd. Is the forum lag getting worse, or is it just me?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114131#post114131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you're saying is that no Infernal's ever become a Devil-Tiger, except for the ones who have.<br /> <br /> There is no &quot;standard&quot; game, TSk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure he means canonically.<br /> I'm pretty sure some players managed to turn their abyssals into deathlords or their dragonblooded into Elemental dragons, but it doesn't mean it's a thing that has ever happened in-setting (which doesn't mean it can't, just that it hasn't).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-16-2014, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T09:52:08-07:00","id":114149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114123#post114123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's cool, but in the standard setting, no Infernal has ever become a devil-tiger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain to me how this is relevant to the question of &quot;can splat X do thing Y and how&quot;? Whether they have yet or not strikes me as a different question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T10:20:35-07:00","id":114174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114149#post114149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain to me how this is relevant to the question of &quot;can splat X do thing Y and how&quot;? Whether they have yet or not strikes me as a different question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it means, at least, that no <u>canon</u> Infernals can do that particular thing, even though one or more might be able to, someday, likely a century or more in the future of the default starting date due to the minimum Essence rating.<br /> <br /> At that Essence, though, it really becomes hard making definitive comparisons between what <u>any</u> Exalts can do, because the charm trees at that level are all incomplete and no real \u201cceiling\u201d on their powers exists. It was suggested in ROTSE that a high-essence Solar could replace the Unconquered Sun, but I don't see us acting like transforming into a Celestial Incarna is part of the capabilities of every Solar, Lunar or Sidereal.<br /> <br /> I just think it'd be better to base comparisons on things that can happen in the run of a typical game, rathe than on crazy things that happen only at high essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T10:21:27-07:00","id":114175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114119#post114119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of devil-tigers is that they keep their humanity while also growing beyond the limitations of it, unlike the yozis which are limited to being alien-minded idiot-savants.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're getting into nuances here, but I'd rather say Devil-Tigers get to choose the specifics of how they lose their humanity, with the added bonus of avoiding the pitfalls involved in becoming an actual Primordial. Because at the end of the day, a guy with his own pantheon of 3CDs and a whole set of Charms that fundamentally alter his basic nature doesn't strike me as particularly human.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm beginning to wonder if calling Infernals &quot;transhuman&quot; (or is it &quot;transhumanist&quot;?) doesn't miss the point of their themes. I mean, WW has a long and proud tradition of having &quot;demonic&quot; splats with weird, transformative, often bizarrely visceral powers - Fomori, Akuma, Belial's Brood, to name a few - but these aren't generally considered transhuman, but rather exploring the themes of corruption through dark power. When you think about it, even Devil-Tigers aren't so much about shedding the limitations of the human form (in the sense that they don't really have a definite edge in this over Yozi Charms, which already deliver in spades), as it is about shedding the limitations imposed on your already supernatural form by your Yozi patrons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T10:30:43-07:00","id":114182,"title":"","content":"All right, so...<br /> <br /> The notion of &quot;transhumanism in Exalted&quot; is completely wrong-headed.<br /> <br /> Firt off: all Exalted are transhuman. <i>Exalted</i>, as a game, is neither a transhumanist <i>game</i>, nor a transhumanist <i>setting</i>, nor has any prevalent <i>theme </i>of transhumanism. <br /> <br /> The first thing to realize is that the notion of &quot;transhumanism in Exalted&quot; as presented in this sort of (recurring) discussion is wrong-headed, because it ultimately comes down to an extremely trite defining criterium, which is itself bound up into a problematic perception of the mechanics of the game: transhumanism is seen as Charms with a duration of &quot;Permanent.&quot; Crowned With Fury, Murder is Meat, Cosmic Transcendence of (Virtue), all that jazz. Even Shintai Charms belong to that category: they reflect a permanent ability to treat your physical shape as something plastic and malleable.<br /> <br /> What it comes down to is that &quot;transhumanism&quot; in Exalted is defined by its fans as &quot;I don't need to spend motes to do it.&quot; This is a problematic perception because it ties into the conception of Charms are individual 'things' that are powered by an inner engine full of discrete 'power units,' and so not truly a part of you. Someone who uses Scar-Writ Saga Shield is transhuman because they permanently make their flesh as hard as steel; someone who uses Spirit-Strengthens-the-Skin is not because they are activating a single power to get a temporary effect. <br /> <br /> This is absurd from an in-setting point of view. A Solar who learns SSS has actually become a hardier person whose flesh is like steel - the fact that this resilience is tiring to sustain and suffers from points of weakness does not change the fact that the Solar has learned, in a very concrete fashion, to change the way their body operates. The fact that Lightning Speed Technique costs &quot;motes&quot; to activate might or might not be a reality in setting, but that doesn't really matter; what it translates practically speaking is that <i>you can go faster than any human being, but that tires you.</i> Wow, that's... literally no different from a futuristic cyborg who would use high-tech implants to run faster. They would probably still get tired. But because Wind-Born Stride has a nice duration of &quot;Permanent,&quot; there is this pervasive idea that it transforms your character in a deeper or more meaningful way than LST. It doesn't. <br /> <br /> Solars are transhuman; in improving their own skills, they actualize themselves in a way beyond human achievement, they become more. They are faster, stronger, their memory works better, they have better sensory faculties, they make faster mental connections between elements of which they have knowledge and intuit greater logical leaps. They transform themselves, progressively, into a person with greater faculties, and remove some of the weaknesses of the human condition, making themselves less vulnerable to disease or wounds - though their progression has, of course, limits, and no Solar can do <i>all of that</i> at once. Solars are transhuman, and so are Dragon-Blooded, Lunars, Abyssals - every Exalt acquires capabilities beyond the human range and progressively make themselves immune to some human vulnerabilities.<br /> <br /> <i>And none of this matters.</i> The Exalted are transhuman, and so what? So is Spider-Man, so is Cyborg, so is a 20th level Fighter in Dungeons and Dragons. This does not matter because <i>their setting is not a transhumanist setting</i>. Because the setting does not give any narrative space to the idea that you can, should, or should not change 'humanity,' improve it, make it more or different from what it is. If Exalted were a transhumanist setting, the Exalted would be the <i>avant-garde,</i> the futuristic 'men of tomorrow' presented as an example of what everyone could become. It would ask questions about whether or not that's a good idea and the practical considerations of implementing such a transition for mankind as a whole. It would allude to the possibility of providing the benefits of Exaltation to the unExalted - and I am not talking about Power-Awarding Prana. <br /> <br /> Infernals, to a very, very limited extent, had glimpses of that. Cecelyne Charms allowed you to change people and societies - to abolish hunger and twist humans into mutated, 'improved'(?) forms. Pyrian Charms allowed you to transform minds... but mostly it was about brainwashing, the same way Cecelyne was mostly about turning people into grotesque abominations suited to a life in an unforgiving wasteland, not about the betterment of mankind. Infernals were transhuman (like everyone else who starts out human and gets incredible power), but they were not <i>transhumanists</i>. <br /> <br /> What Exalted is, however, is a <i>humanist </i>setting. The fact that humanity as a whole cannot acquire the powers of the Exalted is never presented as a bad thing - it is, in fact, never given much thought at all. Exalted does not offer transformation into something that does not suffer from human weaknesses and limits as a solution to mankind's woes; it offers these solutions as being achievable only through human means. How do you solve war? By facilitating international relationships and securing peace between nations. How do you solve hunger? By arranging a better distribution of wealth and produce. By putting an end to the societal conditions that led to starving people. How do you solve sickness? By reducing war so that they are no armies of soldiers shitting in the water supplies! <br /> <br /> Exalted heroes have the great might to effect these changes and better the world, but they are not, inherently, the key to that change. People (mortals and Exalts alike) could improve this situation themselves; it's just that <i>you</i> are given greater power and opportunity to do so. The solution to the world's plight is not to sit around waiting for a supernatural being to cure it; it is to get up and do something about it - and Solars just have greater incentive and opportunity <i>both</i> to do something about it <i>and</i> to get other people to do something about it as well.<br /> <br /> You change things through reason, through the betterment of society, through education and from freaking common sense (&quot;stop shitting in the water&quot; is 'reason' when you first realize that it's the cause of cholera, 'education' when you tell everyone about it, and 'freaking common sense' once everyone does know about it). You change things by helping people achieve their own potential. The most significant Solar Charms when it comes to the bettering of people are the two Training Charms in Lore and War: they do not transform people, they do not mutate them or give them inhuman gifts. They help them achieve their own potential. They help them realize themselves. These Charms have no sustained costs: your Tiger Warriors do not lose their skills once you cease committing motes to them, they remain perfectly accomplished warriors, just as your Lore-trained scholars remained doctors and scientists and thaumaturges and diplomats and what have you. You have made people better: you have spread reason and education.<br /> <br /> There has always been, in the fanbase, the common idea that a way to better the lot of mankind in Creation is to enlighten mortals. That was a transhumanist element, though it was never conceived of as such by most who advanced it, because 'transhumanism' is a loaded world that evokes Cyberpunk 2077 and Eclipse Phase rather than minor magic. It was also a pretty weird and nonsensical idea. There was this &quot;Essence,&quot; this vague power that everyone who mattered in the setting could use, and humans could not, except if they went through a special enlightening process and then they always could forever. Of course having that power would be better than not having it - nevermind that it actually did nothing aside from allow you to skip the fluff of thaumaturgy (and its Resources cost) and just wave your hands and say 'it's done,' or, more problematically, learn Terrestrial Martial Arts and Sorcery. how that's thankfully going away.<br /> <br /> Why thankfully? Because, again, Exalted is not a transhumanist setting. The notion that improving the lot of mankind can be done by giving everyone special magical powers flies completely against the messages and themes of Exalted - it is, in its transhumanist elements, antihumanist. You don't solve the troubles of Creation by giving everyone special magical power; you solve them by facing them in a human way, by finding the human factors at the core of these troubles - greed, apathy, endemic warfare, prejudice, ignorance - and solving them in a human way - with reason and education and humanity.<br /> <br /> A deathlord is like any other warlord, scaled up. He is a conquering man with human greed and human desires, and you solve the problems he pauses in a human manner. Yes, it's scaled up; yes, diplomacy involves Eclipse Oaths and spirit immunities and necromantic binding, and warfare involves armies of zombies and giant lumbering behemoth-corpses, and personal drama involves great passions and excesses and the Curse of ancient gods. But at its core, the Solar facing a deathlord is a human story, solved in a human manner - as presented through the medium of myth and the epic imagery of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> I might have more to say, but this post is already so long no one is going to read it in full, so let this be my conclusion: the fact that individual Exalts have transhuman power matters not one whit. If you want Solars to have transhuman powers, it's all right: they already do. And if you really need these transhuman powers to feel like permanent changes to your being by having no mote cost, that's all right: Ex3 will have plenty of entry-level, Permanent duration Charms. But it won't matter. Exalted is not a transhumanist story. It has no interest whatsoever in the questions and concerns of a transhumanist story. It is profondly, deeply humanistic, and the greatness and magic of its Chosen heroes serves only as an epic medium, a larger-than-life portrait, of its humanist concerns. It's a game that is about <i>you, today</i>, your flaws and your merits and what you can accomplish with them - not about how you can transcend these flaws into something more.<br /> <br /> And that's why it's so damn good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces 