e problematically, learn Terrestrial Martial Arts and Sorcery. how that's thankfully going away.<br /> <br /> Why thankfully? Because, again, Exalted is not a transhumanist setting. The notion that improving the lot of mankind can be done by giving everyone special magical powers flies completely against the messages and themes of Exalted - it is, in its transhumanist elements, antihumanist. You don't solve the troubles of Creation by giving everyone special magical power; you solve them by facing them in a human way, by finding the human factors at the core of these troubles - greed, apathy, endemic warfare, prejudice, ignorance - and solving them in a human way - with reason and education and humanity.<br /> <br /> A deathlord is like any other warlord, scaled up. He is a conquering man with human greed and human desires, and you solve the problems he pauses in a human manner. Yes, it's scaled up; yes, diplomacy involves Eclipse Oaths and spirit immunities and necromantic binding, and warfare involves armies of zombies and giant lumbering behemoth-corpses, and personal drama involves great passions and excesses and the Curse of ancient gods. But at its core, the Solar facing a deathlord is a human story, solved in a human manner - as presented through the medium of myth and the epic imagery of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> I might have more to say, but this post is already so long no one is going to read it in full, so let this be my conclusion: the fact that individual Exalts have transhuman power matters not one whit. If you want Solars to have transhuman powers, it's all right: they already do. And if you really need these transhuman powers to feel like permanent changes to your being by having no mote cost, that's all right: Ex3 will have plenty of entry-level, Permanent duration Charms. But it won't matter. Exalted is not a transhumanist story. It has no interest whatsoever in the questions and concerns of a transhumanist story. It is profondly, deeply humanistic, and the greatness and magic of its Chosen heroes serves only as an epic medium, a larger-than-life portrait, of its humanist concerns. It's a game that is about <i>you, today</i>, your flaws and your merits and what you can accomplish with them - not about how you can transcend these flaws into something more.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> And that's why it's so damn good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I just...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i819.photobucket.com/albums/zz119/fajaraseoul/Post%20love/catLovePost-1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> ... go on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T13:57:42-07:00","id":114319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism#post113651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an old quote somewhere on the old forums about a Solar who goes searching for cosmic transcendence and eventually figures out that he already has it by virtue of being a Solar. This has always struck me as a cop-out when compared to &quot;real&quot; transhumanists who have mechanical support for their transformations into &quot;something else&quot; like the Infernals and Alchemicals. Could someone explain to me where this position comes from? I have difficulty seeing how a Solar can be called transhuman any more than Batman or Son Goku can be called such.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mostly a problem of genre.<br /> <br /> When Adam Jessen is almost beaten to death and survives because much of his organic parts are replaced with cybornetics, the story presumes a clear dividing line between what's human and what isn't. Those fleshy, organic legs he was born with represent the abilities of standard humanity; the plastic, prosthetic ones he's given can overcome the limits of those fleshy legs.<br /> <br /> Cybernetic legs transcend fleshy legs. Adam now gets to do things humans can't do... but Adam is still human. In that specific paradox is a transhuman; a human who has somehow surpassed the limits of humanity.<br /> <br /> Solars don't transcend a predefined humanity. Even when they leap over mountains, they remain firmly within the setting's concept of 'totally human.' Nor do they suggest a possible posthuman existence. If you took the conceptual underpinnings of Deus Ex and applied them to Solars then Solars are transhuman. Then again, if you took Deus Ex's conceptual underpinnings and applied them to beastmen, those wouldn't be humans at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T15:59:45-07:00","id":114380,"title":"","content":"Transhumanist fiction is about asking how advances in technology will change what it means to be human. For example, what would you be like if you could live forever, walk on the outside of an asteroid without a space-suit while you feel the solar wind on metallo-organic carapace, see radio waves, terraform worlds with the aid of your multiple idiot-savant clone minds that only exist inside your head and have been created for this specific task after which they will be erased, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Exalted answers this with &quot;Well, pretty much the same as you are now&quot; so it's not really transhumanist although it certainly could be if one wanted it to. Lunars could be said to have a transhumanist thing going on, but it's really more of a God-Monster thing. I suppose the same could be said of Infernals. The reason I'm saying this is because transhumanist literature generally focuses on the question &quot;What will we become?&quot; and Exalted just states &quot;This is what you will become&quot;. Although Infernals doing their own thing are an exception I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T12:19:36-07:00","id":114871,"title":"","content":"So, people are free to disagree with me, but I think Solars DO have a transhumanistic path, one that is much more truly 'transhuman' than anything in Infernals.<br /> <br /> It's called Wyld Shaping Technique. Namely the ability to just say &quot;Fuck it all&quot; and run off into the Wyld and create your own whole new world abandoning humanity and Creation to it's fate/Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/726-amine-hsu","name":"Amine Hsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar726_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T12:40:24-07:00","id":114877,"title":"","content":"That's not really transhumanism so much as it's just a change of location. Nothing about the human condition, or even your condition, really changes from just taking Bikini Bottom and pushing it somewhere else. Otherwise Autochthonia would be a transhuman society, which it isn't.<br /> <br /> Transhumanism, as I noted earlier in the thread, has a broad variety of definitions that all get lumped together, but all of them have to do with a fundamental change in the state of being human somehow. WST doesn't really accomplish that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T13:01:33-07:00","id":114896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amine Hsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114871#post114871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's called Wyld Shaping Technique. Namely the ability to just say &quot;Fuck it all&quot; and run off into the Wyld and create your own whole new world abandoning humanity and Creation to it's fate/Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, at about thirty square miles per use, that would take...?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Expanded thought: it would seem to me that the impulse to say &quot;I don't care what happens here anymore&quot; and going off somewhere else is not so much transhuman as... the exact reason that humans live anywhere other than central Africa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T13:06:06-07:00","id":114902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113651-solar-transhumanism?p=114877#post114877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really transhumanism so much as it's just a change of location. Nothing about the human condition, or even your condition, really changes from just taking Bikini Bottom and pushing it somewhere else. Otherwise Autochthonia would be a transhuman society, which it isn't.<br /> <br /> Transhumanism, as I noted earlier in the thread, has a broad variety of definitions that all get lumped together, but all of them have to do with a fundamental change in the state of being human somehow. WST doesn't really accomplish that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it does create something of a post-scarcity environment if any shortage in resources can be corrected in a manner of hours. This does remove an important limitation on the human condition. In general, I'd argue that being able to create things, even life, with the power of your mind would alter the human condition significantly.<br /> <br /> Still, technically, it's not really more transhuman than a Charm that makes you immune to all non-magical poisons and toxins. Just more overt in how it makes you stand out among humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T13:58:07-07:00","id":114928,"title":"","content":"You could tell a transhumanist story using nothing but the golden Ancestor Sashes from An-Teng or the panoply of artifacts a Gunzosha soldier uses, but the default assumption is that you're not doing this because that's not what Exalted is about. If you're running a campaign about what it means to be a Gunzosha soldier then maybe that's different, but most games are going to be about using the Gunzosha armor to accomplish some end. A story about Major Kusanagi wondering if she's human or machine is transhumanist fiction, a story about Major Kusanagi punching people in the face is an action movie. Exalted tends to identify with the action movie path.<br /> <br /> So, yes, WST lets you take off to deep space and make your own society in the same way that a collective of people might live in an asteroid and redefine themselves with radical changes accomplished by nanoassemblers and casual psycho-surgery, but generally WST is going to make something that's recognizably Creation with people that consider themselves the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/407-ithle","name":"Ithle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T07:24:23-07:00","id":116491,"title":"","content":"I think that transhumanism (in the sense of transforming the human condition) is an entirely valid goal for an Exalted character, since fighting against the limitations of human condition is part of the heroic narrative (you can argue that eg. anyone going on an enlightenment-quest or the like is seeking a transhuman goal, especially if your character is seeking to become a Bodhisattva or the like and spread enlightenment to everyone.) However, <i>achieving</i> it would be the end of your story; the goal they are seeking would be a world with no need of heroes. (In practical terms it would probably be more of a &quot;distant ideal&quot; and not an achievable goal -- &quot;eliminate all warfare forever&quot; or even &quot;eliminate death&quot; is very much a valid goal in a heroic narrative, but it is probably not something you are going to see actually happen in play.)<br /> <br /> And it's not like they're going to have transhumanism powers in that line any more than there are specific &quot;live happily ever after&quot; powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}